{"run_id": "r-f0611f390ade-1", "task_id": "retry-q2-t0448-t0001", "trace_id": "retry-q2-t0448-trace0001", "member_id": "s1-r1-m07", "planned_activity_id": "retry-q2-t0448-p0001", "phase_id": "phase2", "workday": 4, "simulation_time": "2025-05-08T13:00:00.009000+08:00", "workflow_id": "software_feature", "call_id": "tool-7ea0abee597b455699f71072286451fc", "from_state": "issue_created", "tool_name": "design_document", "event_type": "tool_call", "to_state": "designed", "arguments": {"content": "Design document for compute(a, b) product feature.\n\n## Overview\nImplement a public function `compute(a, b)` in `src/main.py` that returns the product of two finite numeric inputs.\n\n## Requirements (from issue f2c5fc2cd26d)\n- `compute(2, 3)` must return `6`.\n- Support zero, negative and fractional values (e.g. `compute(0, 5) == 0`, `compute(-2, 3) == -6`, `compute(2.5, 4) == 10.0`).\n- Inputs must be finite numbers; non-numeric or non-finite inputs (NaN, +/-inf) must be rejected with a clear error (TypeError/ValueError).\n- Validate behavior with `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python checks/public_check.py`.\n- Build with `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src`.\n- Fixture variation 2.\n\n## Design\n- Module: `src/main.py`.\n- Function signature: `def compute(a, b):`.\n- Validation strategy:\n  1. Accept `int`, `float`, and `numbers.Real`-compatible numeric types (excluding `bool`, which is technically an int subclass but semantically not a numeric input for this feature).\n  2. Reject non-numeric types with `TypeError`.\n  3. Reject non-finite values (`math.isnan`, `math.isinf`) with `ValueError`.\n- Core computation: return `a * b` after validation, preserving Python's natural numeric semantics (int*int -> int, float involved -> float).\n- No external dependencies; standard library only (`math`, `numbers`).\n\n## Verification plan\n- Run `checks/public_check.py` (public behavioral check) \u2014 must pass.\n- Run bytecode compilation build: `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src` \u2014 must succeed.\n- Then proceed to local simulated review (pull_request) and approval phases.\n\n## Risks\n- bool inputs: excluded explicitly to keep semantics strict; bool is not considered a valid numeric input here.\n- Very large integers: Python handles arbitrary precision; no overflow handling needed.\n- Float precision: standard IEEE-754 semantics apply; no rounding beyond Python defaults.", "input_artifact_id": "f2c5fc2cd26d"}, "result": {"tool_name": "design_document", "message": "design document created", "output_artifact_ids": ["eef8319d76ab"], "output_paths": ["artifacts/eef8319d76ab.md"], "evidence_level": "simulation_only", "business_status": "not_measured", "payload": "Design document for compute(a, b) product feature.\n\n## Overview\nImplement a public function `compute(a, b)` in `src/main.py` that returns the product of two finite numeric inputs.\n\n## Requirements (from issue f2c5fc2cd26d)\n- `compute(2, 3)` must return `6`.\n- Support zero, negative and fractional values (e.g. `compute(0, 5) == 0`, `compute(-2, 3) == -6`, `compute(2.5, 4) == 10.0`).\n- Inputs must be finite numbers; non-numeric or non-finite inputs (NaN, +/-inf) must be rejected with a clear error (TypeError/ValueError).\n- Validate behavior with `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python checks/public_check.py`.\n- Build with `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src`.\n- Fixture variation 2.\n\n## Design\n- Module: `src/main.py`.\n- Function signature: `def compute(a, b):`.\n- Validation strategy:\n  1. Accept `int`, `float`, and `numbers.Real`-compatible numeric types (excluding `bool`, which is technically an int subclass but semantically not a numeric input for this feature).\n  2. Reject non-numeric types with `TypeError`.\n  3. Reject non-finite values (`math.isnan`, `math.isinf`) with `ValueError`.\n- Core computation: return `a * b` after validation, preserving Python's natural numeric semantics (int*int -> int, float involved -> float).\n- No external dependencies; standard library only (`math`, `numbers`).\n\n## Verification plan\n- Run `checks/public_check.py` (public behavioral check) \u2014 must pass.\n- Run bytecode compilation build: `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src` \u2014 must succeed.\n- Then proceed to local simulated review (pull_request) and approval phases.\n\n## Risks\n- bool inputs: excluded explicitly to keep semantics strict; bool is not considered a valid numeric input here.\n- Very large integers: Python handles arbitrary precision; no overflow handling needed.\n- Float precision: standard IEEE-754 semantics apply; no rounding beyond Python defaults.", "output_paths_kind": "read_only_capture_evidence", "business_path": null, "workspace": "/Users/ayang/Desktop/project_work/Chimera/docs/dataset-evaluation/reports/stage2/full-from-scratch-20261015/q2-q3/failure-rerun-20261016/tasks/q2-t0448/study/workspaces/retry-q2-t0448-t0001", "execution_environment": {"cwd": "/Users/ayang/Desktop/project_work/Chimera/docs/dataset-evaluation/reports/stage2/full-from-scratch-20261015/q2-q3/failure-rerun-20261016/tasks/q2-t0448/study/workspaces/retry-q2-t0448-t0001", "python_executable": "/opt/anaconda3/bin/python", "default_build_command": "/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src", "build_kind": "python_bytecode_compilation", "optional_modules": {"pytest": true, "build": false, "pip": true, "setuptools": true}}}, "status": "success", "schema_version": "chimera-event/1", "event_seq": 9, "event_id": "126ca969b73e4240ab319f02abf3f830", "wall_time_utc": "2026-10-16T07:52:17.025512+00:00"}
